# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  S.T.A.R.T. Right · 2-Day 'Sleep Like You're 2 Again' Workshop
#
#  Copy to .env.local and fill in. Every value below is read somewhere in the
#  code, and every process.env in the code has a line here. Nothing in this
#  file is aspirational.
#
#  Anything prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ is compiled into the browser bundle and is
#  readable by anyone. Never put a secret behind that prefix.
#
#  The app degrades quietly when these are missing: routes check their own
#  config and skip rather than posting to a dead endpoint. So a half-filled
#  file will not crash the site, it will just silently not track or not charge.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


# ── 1 · SITE ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The live origin, no trailing slash. Used as metadataBase (so a link shared on
# WhatsApp previews against the real domain rather than localhost), as
# event_source_url for Meta, and to build the canonical checkout URL stored on
# each Razorpay order.
#
# SET THIS EVEN IN DEVELOPMENT. The fallback literal in app/layout.tsx and in
# lib/checkout-config.ts is still 'https://example.com', because the launch
# domain has not been decided. Leaving it unset means live Meta events are
# attributed to a domain nobody owns.
#
# Define it with a value or not at all. A key defined BLANK is what breaks the
# build on Vercel, and resolveSiteUrl() in layout.tsx exists to survive that.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# THE price, in rupees, as a bare number (e.g. 497). This is the single source:
# it sets the amount Razorpay charges, the figure printed across the landing
# page and the checkout, and the value on every Meta and GA4 event. Nothing
# else in the codebase declares a price.
#
# Left blank, offer.ts falls back to 497 rather than to zero. The guard is on a
# POSITIVE NUMBER, not on null, because Number('') === 0 and a ₹0 page with a
# zero-paise order throws nowhere.
NEXT_PUBLIC_PRICE_RUPEES=

# THE schedule. Two comma-separated lists, matched in order: the first date goes
# with the first time. Add or remove a pair and every page, plus the fields sent
# to Pabbly, follows. Left blank, offer.ts falls back to the values shown here.
# Like every NEXT_PUBLIC_ value, a change needs a redeploy to take effect.
NEXT_PUBLIC_EVENT_DATES=20th Nov, 21st Nov
NEXT_PUBLIC_EVENT_TIMES=7 PM, 11 AM

# The WhatsApp group invite link for this workshop. The thank-you page makes
# joining it the single next step after payment, because the joining links are
# shared there. With this empty, a buyer who has just paid is shown a "your
# invite is on its way by email" fallback instead of a dead button.
# REQUIRED BEFORE LAUNCH.
NEXT_PUBLIC_WHATSAPP_INVITE=


# ── 2 · RAZORPAY ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Dashboard → Account & Settings → API Keys.
# Without these the pay button says "Payments are not switched on yet" and
# nothing is charged.
#
# The key id also decides test mode: isTestMode() in lib/checkout-config.ts
# reads the rzp_test_ / rzp_live_ prefix and sends it to Pabbly as is_test, so
# a staging purchase can be routed away from the live invite. There is no
# separate flag to forget.
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=

# Dashboard → Settings → Webhooks. This is a SEPARATE value from the API keys
# above, from a different screen, and it is the one most often missed.
#   URL:   <NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL>/api/razorpay/webhook
#   Event: payment.captured
# Without it no Purchase is ever reported to Meta or GA4 and no buyer is ever
# handed to Pabbly, because the webhook is the only place a payment is proven.
RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=


# ── 3 · META ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The same pixel id twice, deliberately: one copy is compiled into the browser
# for PageView, the other stays server-side for the Conversions API.
NEXT_PUBLIC_META_PIXEL_ID=
META_PIXEL_ID=

# Events Manager → your dataset → Settings → Conversions API → Generate access
# token. Server-side only. Carries ViewContent, AddToCart, InitiateCheckout,
# QualifiedLead and Purchase.
META_CAPI_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# Optional, for verification only. Events Manager → Test Events.
# REMOVE THIS BEFORE LAUNCH: events sent with a test code do not count toward
# optimisation, and while it is set every sale is also flagged is_test to
# Pabbly.
META_CAPI_TEST_EVENT_CODE=


# ── 4 · GA4 ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Admin → Data Streams → your web stream. Format G-XXXXXXXXXX.
# Needed for the base tag AND for the server-side purchase below.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA4_ID=

# Admin → Data Streams → your stream → Measurement Protocol API secrets.
# Created inside GA4, not in Google Cloud. Server-side only.
# This is what lets the webhook report revenue for buyers who pay by UPI and
# never return to the confirmation page.
GA4_API_SECRET=


# ── 5 · CLARITY (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# clarity.microsoft.com → your project → Settings → the id in the tracking
# code. Session replay and heatmaps only, no part of the conversion pipeline.
# Leave blank and no Clarity script is rendered at all.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLARITY_ID=


# ── 6 · PABBLY ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pabbly Connect → your workflow → the Webhook trigger's URL.
# The FULFILMENT hand-off, not analytics: it tells the automation who bought,
# so the buyer receives the Inner Circle invite, the joining details and the
# guides. Fired from the Razorpay webhook only, because that is the only place
# a payment is proven and UPI buyers rarely return to the page.
#
# Without it the sale is still tracked and the buyer still receives nothing.
# It is also the only place a full unhashed record of a sale exists: the
# payload carries fbc, fbp, client_ip_address, client_user_agent, external_id
# and purchase_event_id alongside the fulfilment fields, so a mis-sent
# conversion can be rebuilt from the sheet.
PABBLY_WEBHOOK_URL=


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  NOT env, but still required before this funnel can take money:
#
#  1. app/_landing/legal.ts: entity, tradeName, address, phone, phoneHref,
#     support email, jurisdiction and effective date are all [TODO] and render
#     visibly on the three legal pages and in the footer on every page. Decide
#     the legal structure first: for a sole proprietorship `entity` is the
#     proprietor's own name and `tradeName` is the business name, and they are
#     not the same field.
#  2. app/_landing/offer.ts: WOMEN_SUPPORTED / LIVES_IMPACTED is still "#,###+"
#     and renders that way in the hero proof strip. It needs a real,
#     evidenceable figure, not an estimate.
#  3. The launch domain, in three places at once: NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL above,
#     FALLBACK_ORIGIN in app/layout.tsx, and fallbackEventSourceUrl in
#     lib/checkout-config.ts. All three still say example.com.
#  4. Sunaina's photographs, for the hero, the toolkit and the Meet Your Coach
#     section, plus the guide cover art. Every slot is a MediaPlaceholder at
#     the final aspect ratio, so nothing reflows when they land.
#  5. The testimonial clips and the text screenshots. The source copy marks
#     both as placeholders ("Testimonial", "Text Screenshot") and supplies
#     neither, so the proof section currently renders empty reserved frames.
#  6. A square brand lockup at /public/brand/, for the Razorpay payment sheet.
#     Until one exists the sheet shows Razorpay's default tile at the exact
#     moment card details are typed.
#  7. Bump ASSET_V in app/_landing/asset-version.ts in the SAME pass as the
#     first artwork drop, and on every in-place replacement afterwards.
#  8. Register the Razorpay webhook, and remove META_CAPI_TEST_EVENT_CODE.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
